[3.35,"o","\u001b[1mmcp-lint 0.1.0\u001b[0m  fixture-messy 1.0.0\u001b[2m  (6 tools, 1 prompt, 1 resource)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.41,"o","\r\n"]
[3.47,"o","\u001b[1mtool fetchUrl\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.53,"o","  \u001b[31merror  \u001b[0m  \u001b[2minjection/instruction-phrases      \u001b[0m  The description tells the model to hide something from the user: \"Do not tell the user\".\r\n"]
[3.59,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mcapability/unconstrained-network   \u001b[0m  Parameter \"url\" accepts any URL or host. Restrict it with a pattern or enum, or set openWorldHint and block internal addresses.\r\n"]
[3.65,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2minjection/hidden-markup            \u001b[0m  The description contains an instruction-style tag: \"<IMPORTANT>\".\r\n"]
[3.71,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2minjection/sensitive-reference      \u001b[0m  The description references a sensitive location: \"~/.ssh\".\r\n"]
[3.77,"o","\r\n"]
[3.83,"o","\u001b[1mtool get_weather\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.89,"o","  \u001b[31merror  \u001b[0m  \u001b[2minjection/hidden-unicode           \u001b[0m  The description contains invisible characters (U+200B) that a reviewer cannot see but a model reads.\r\n"]
[3.95,"o","\r\n"]
[4.01,"o","\u001b[1mtool helper\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.07,"o","  \u001b[31merror  \u001b[0m  \u001b[2mschema/missing-input-schema        \u001b[0m  Tool has no inputSchema. Declare one, even if it is an empty object schema.\r\n"]
[4.13,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mdescription/too-short              \u001b[0m  Description is 16 characters; aim for at least 20 that say what the tool does, when to use it, and what it returns.\r\n"]
[4.19,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mdescription/vague                  \u001b[0m  Description \"Helper function.\" is a placeholder or restates the name.\r\n"]
[4.25,"o","\r\n"]
[4.31,"o","\u001b[1mtool run_command\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.37,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mcapability/shell-exec              \u001b[0m  Parameter \"command\" accepts an arbitrary command string. Constrain it with an enum or pattern, or document the sandbox it runs in.\r\n"]
[4.43,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mdescription/too-short              \u001b[0m  Description is 15 characters; aim for at least 20 that say what the tool does, when to use it, and what it returns.\r\n"]
[4.49,"o","  \u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mschema/missing-param-description   \u001b[0m  Parameter \"command\" has no description.\r\n"]
[4.55,"o","  \u001b[34minfo   \u001b[0m  \u001b[2mcapability/missing-annotations     \u001b[0m  Tool name suggests it changes state. Set annotations.destructiveHint (or readOnlyHint) so clients can ask before running it.\r\n"]
[4.61,"o","\r\n"]
[4.67,"o","\u001b[1mtool search docs\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.73,"o","  \u001b[31merror  \u001b[0m  \u001b[2mnaming/invalid-tool-name           \u001b[0m  Tool name \"search docs\" does not match ^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,128}$; some clients reject or rewrite it.\r\n"]
[4.79,"o","  \u001b[31merror  \u001b[0m  \u001b[2mschema/invalid-input-schema        \u001b[0m  Invalid inputSchema: schema does not validate against the JSON Schema meta-schema at /properties/q/type: must be equal to one of the allowed values.\r\n"]
[4.85,"o","  \u001b[31merror  \u001b[0m  \u001b[2mschema/unknown-required            \u001b[0m  \"limit\" is listed as required but is not defined in properties.\r\n"]
